# Integrity lock for the evaluator-owned files of the LOCAL LIVE-MODEL
# SUPERVISOR ACCEPTANCE GATE (spec: /tmp/lv-supervisor-local-acceptance-spec.md,
# sha256 3ed295730058e053a001d831dc5ed937e860d0fca6dae2ae7b3311ac80de337a;
# architecture: /tmp/lv-autonomous-live-content-architecture.md, sha256
# 4704227a99b84089a7fead2ed39b2b605b884edf903d9d65261c930f78071758).
#
# SIXTH EVAL-OWNER FREEZE: re-frozen after a focused live reproduction proved a
# CHECKER SELECTOR defect. Production was correct and unchanged; two frozen
# checks were reading the wrong child out of a SHARED evidence log.
#
# THE DEFECT — SELECTOR AMBIGUITY UNDER BASELINE NOISE. The parent-owned spawn
# log records every node child the run tree starts, and the five baseline gates
# run the repository's OWN suites. `npm run test:automation` alone drives
# fifteen fixture `record-candidate-outcome` coordinator children
# (tests/automation/*.eval.mjs) long before the supervisor writes its own
# outcome. `local-acceptance-negatives.eval.mjs` selected that record twice with
# `.find(entry => entry.argv.includes('record-candidate-outcome'))`, so N4-reason
# and N4-durable both inspected record 0 — `--reason "fixture candidate failed"`,
# 24 characters, no `--topic-key` — and reported RED. The run's OWN record was
# record 15: `--key` equal to the ledger `run_id`, `--topic-key` equal to the
# ledger `topic_key`, `--outcome DISCARDED_PRE_PR`, a reason at the 512-character
# bound ending in the literal `…[truncated]`, and `--repo` appended last. The
# durable candidate-state issue stored exactly that reason and `Last outcome
# DISCARDED_PRE_PR`. Reported scratch N3 run: `runRow.error` 5258 characters,
# reason 511, 16 record-candidate-outcome entries in the shared log. The eval
# owner's own re-run against production e8e4b32 reproduced it exactly (error
# 5262, reason 512, 16 entries, naive first-match = fixture record 0
# `blog-isolated-run` / 24 characters, exact selector = record 15).
#
# THE EVALUATOR-ONLY FIX.
#
# (1) NEW eval-owned helper `helpers/acceptance-selectors.mjs` (the manifest set
#     grows to 16; `local-acceptance.eval.mjs` stays within its 400-line budget,
#     which is why the selectors are a split rather than more of
#     acceptance-evidence.mjs). `candidateOutcomeRecord()` selects THE record
#     whose `--key` equals the run row's run_id AND whose `--topic-key` equals
#     the run row's topic_key AND whose `--outcome` is the terminal under test,
#     and FAILS BY NAME on zero matches and on more than one. The subcommand is
#     read positionally (argv[2]), so an entry that merely carries the string in
#     a `--reason` is not a candidate, and flags are parsed pairwise so a value
#     spelled like a flag is consumed as a value, never re-read as one (a bare
#     indexOf would let a decoy overwrite the run key). N4-reason and N4-durable
#     now share ONE memoized selection, so the bounded reason and the durable
#     ladder value are provably read off the same child.
#
# (2) AUDIT of every other spawn-log selector for the same baseline-noise
#     ambiguity, tightening only where a selector could actually read fixture
#     noise. `local-acceptance-mutations.eval.mjs` M138-shape took `.at(-1)` over
#     every blog-lint child; `npm run test:supervisor` drives fixture linters
#     (tests/supervisor/contracts.test.mjs), one of them with ABSOLUTE
#     `--posts`/`--businesses`, so on the GENERATION_FAILED_PRE_PR terminal
#     M138-red also accepts — where the supervisor never lints — the last entry
#     is fixture noise that satisfies "pre-#138 shape". That direction is a false
#     GREEN, and it is now `supervisorLintInvocation()`: the run's own lint is
#     selected by the exact trusted repoRoot script the host invokes (identical
#     before and after #138, which moved only the cwd and the data paths), with
#     zero and multiple both failing. Selectors left UNCHANGED, with cause:
#     `lintInvocation()` (N3-shape, C2, N5-live5, PC3) discriminates on canonical
#     containment in `<state>/work`, and every fixture linter runs from `$TMPDIR`
#     or the double's own `<root>/ingest-wt-*`, so noise is excluded — and the
#     assertLintShape that follows asserts exact script identity, so noise could
#     only fail loudly, never pass; N1-order already discriminates host from
#     fixture coordinators on `samePath(cwd, clone)`; `baselineSteps`/`C2` read an
#     ORDERED npm-step projection where fixture children contribute no npm run
#     steps; `recordOutcomeThroughSeam` parses argv the evaluator's own seam
#     captured from production, not the shared log.
#
# (3) DETERMINISTIC REGRESSION PS1–PS5 in local-acceptance-probes.eval.mjs — no
#     model token, no network, before any credential use, so it runs even on a
#     baseline RED tree. It replays the observed noise (fixture records ahead of
#     the run's own, including one sharing the run key with a different topic and
#     one sharing the topic key with a different run) and proves: the naive
#     first-match selector really does take a decoy (control), the exact selector
#     takes record 15 with its 511-character truncated reason and appended
#     `--repo`; a wrong run key, wrong topic key, wrong outcome, and an absent
#     topic key are each refused BY NAME; a duplicate is refused as ambiguous;
#     the pairwise/positional parse survives a `--reason` spelled `--key` and a
#     `--reason` spelled exactly like the subcommand; and a log of fixture
#     linters only is refused instead of passing as the pre-#138 shape. Each
#     direction was proven discriminating by mutating the selector back to the
#     naive form and observing the matching probe fail.
#
# The file set is 16 eval-owned files. Every file below is eval-owned and FROZEN.
#
# These files are FROZEN. The implementation builder must not edit, weaken,
# delete, re-scope, or restage any of them. Maker != checker: any change to an
# eval-owned path is a spec/eval-owner change and an automatic FAIL of the
# acceptance review until the eval owner re-freezes.
#
# Verify (from the repository root; every line must print OK and exit 0):
